Here you find the original program from Sverre Froyen
dated from 1982 with some minor modifications so that
it would run on a cdc205, a supercomputer with 
17 Linpack Mflops, same as a good 2011 cell phone.

It still compiles, complaining about Holerith constants
and still runs.  Oviously the old code does not
have all the options and capabilities, so a
compatible atom.dat file is provided.

Just compile

ifx atomsve.f date.f -o atom.exe

or

gfortran atomsve.f date.f -o atom.exe

run the executable, and check the result in the file atom.out.




